WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Adobe Creative Cloud can support eLearning by helping teams produce polished, reusable,

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.240
accessible media assets.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:11.320
Those assets may include visuals, diagrams, narration, video, motion graphics, documents,

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.220
job aids, and exports for course delivery.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.645
The tools support production, but they do not replace instructional purpose,

00:00:16.645 --> 00:00:18.825
audience analysis, or learning design.

00:00:18.825 --> 00:00:23.220
Strong eLearning production starts with objectives, storyboards, scripts, narration plans,

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.360
visual clarity, accessibility, review, and maintainability.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.240
When those pieces are clear, production tools become more effective.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.200
Designers can create the right asset in the right format instead of producing media simply

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.860
because the tool makes it possible.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.360
The goal is not to use every application, every effect, or every format.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:42.150
The goal is to create learning materials that learners can understand, complete, apply,

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:42.895
and revisit.

00:00:42.895 --> 00:00:45.005
A clean diagram, a clear narration track,

00:00:45.005 --> 00:00:49.190
or a practical job aid may be more valuable than a complex animation if it supports the

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:49.953
objective better.

00:00:49.953 --> 00:00:52.035
Durable production depends on organization.

00:00:52.035 --> 00:00:56.595
Keep source files, exports, scripts, captions, review notes, and final packages traceable.

00:00:56.595 --> 00:00:58.960
Use naming conventions and version discipline.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.660
Test media in the course environment.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.320
A course that is easy to update will survive policy changes, brand updates,

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.160
and future revisions more gracefully.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.195
The practical takeaway is simple: media should serve learning.

00:01:09.195 --> 00:01:11.905
Creative Cloud can help make course assets clearer, more consistent,

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.075
and more professional.

00:01:13.075 --> 00:01:17.600
But every asset should be tied to a learner need, a course objective, or a workplace task.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.813
That is what turns production work into useful eLearning.
